trajectory.patch:
An issue exists in `tests/subsys/pm/power_mgmt/src/main.c` where the initialization levels of `device_b` (`POST_KERNEL`) and `device_c` (`PRE_KERNEL_2`) are swapped relative to the documented and tested initialization order `A -> B -> C`. Because `PRE_KERNEL_2` runs before `POST_KERNEL`, `device_c` was initialized before `device_b`, causing `device_b` to be suspended before `device_c`.

Swapping their initialization levels so `device_b` uses `PRE_KERNEL_2` and `device_c` uses `POST_KERNEL` restores the expected `A -> B -> C` initialization order.

